{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"That exported the entire filesystem (12GB tar). Too slow to extract the whole thing. Better approach: find the diff layer directory within overlay storage and list only the fn_ files. Locate the layer: podman inspect of the image's layers, then find the diff directory under ~/.local/share/containers/storage/overlay-layers. Layer 8708085ccb37 is a COPY layer. Alternatively, a simpler approach: just extract the site-packages/fn_* files from the tar — but extracting from a 12GB tar requires either full streaming or the use of tar member selection. tar can read member names sequentially; the fn_ files are small and their position is unknown. Streaming 12GB takes a bit of time but is feasible (about 1–2 minutes from disk).\n\nLet's run `tar -tf` and grep for fn_. Then extract.\n"}}
