{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Does fn_*.py not exist at all in the flattened fs (other than torch samples)? But the COPY layer did add 4.61kB. Hmm — is podman export actually flattening all layers? For a *container* created from an image, `podman export` should include everything. Unless the files in the COPY layer were subsequently deleted... no, no deletion was done afterwards.\n\nWait — maybe the copy destination wasn't the root of site-packages: \"COPY dir:e37e... in /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/\" — copying to a directory with a trailing slash. The files should end up inside there. Hmm, but what if the COPY source was empty, or contained only directories? 4.61kB of \"changes\" could be just directories + metadata. Or maybe the files have different names. Let me check the overlay's diff directory directly: identify the layer diff that contains the fn files. Search overlay storage."}}
